# bounded-context isolation gate allowlist.
#
# The gate (tests/Unit/Shared/Architecture/BoundedContextGateTest.php) fails the
# build when a file in one business context imports another business context's
# `Domain\` or `Application\` namespace — see the Level 1 rule in
# docs/rules/database.md#bounded-context-data-isolation-modular-monolith.
# `Erpify\Shared\…` is always importable (shared kernel) and never needs listing.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Three entry forms:
#
#   <relative/path.php>
#       Exempt the whole importer file. Coarse escape hatch — prefer a seam
#       entry so a *new* bad import in the same file is still caught.
#
#   <relative/path.php> => <Imported\Fqcn>
#       Exempt one specific (importer file, imported FQCN) seam. Preferred.
#
#   * => <Imported\Fqcn>
#       A globally published seam: a context's published Application service
#       interface or an integration-event class, importable from any context.
#
# Paths are POSIX, relative to api/, with no leading slash. Adding an entry is a
# deliberate, reviewable exception: the only legitimate reasons are a published
# cross-context seam (Application service interface / integration event) or a
# coupling explicitly justified in an ADR.

# Bank → BankAccount referential-integrity check. BankDeleter (Bank/Application)
# consumes the BankAccountRepository *interface* to block deleting a bank that
# still has accounts (clean 409 before the FK fires). Blessed by
# docs/adr/bank-bankaccount-modeling.md (inverse direction, "el patrón correcto").
src/Backoffice/Bank/Application/BankDeleter.php => Erpify\Backoffice\BankAccount\Domain\Repository\BankAccountRepository
